5. Two human players, X and O.
6. X moves first.
7. Valid moves alternate.
8. Occupied squares cannot be played and rejected attempts do not consume the turn.
9. Normal row/column/diagonal wins terminate immediately.
10. Normal wins have precedence over Komi, including move 9.
11. If the board becomes full without a normal winning line, O wins the Komi tiebreak.
12. Terminal states reject further moves.
13. Play Again resets to an empty board with X to move.
14. UI announces exactly:
    - Player X won
    - Player O won
    - Player O won with Komi

