Our current proposed rule is:

1. Normal tic-tac-toe three-in-a-row wins immediately.
2. A move may only be made in an empty square; an invalid click does not consume the turn.
3. If all 9 squares become occupied without a three-in-a-row winner, the player with fewer marks wins.
4. Since X moves first, a full board contains 5 X marks and 4 O marks, so in that case O wins via the "Komi" / tie-break rule.
5. After a terminal result, no further moves are accepted.
6. The UI should announce whether X won, O won, or O won via Komi.
7. The user can start another game after the result.

